      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TRUE SPIRIT (6) produced a fair effort on debut last time out when 6 lengths from the winner in sixth at Cranbourne over 1000m. Trials prior had been good and this is much easier. COCO LA BOSS (7) is a filly by Farnan out of French Boss who will be improved off a trial placing. From a canny stable that can produce one on debut, so watch market. CHASING ATLANTIS (2) is a three-start maiden who could only manage to finish seventh at her latest appearance over 1000m at Ballarat. Down a rung or two here and draws the coveted inside alley. MANHATTAN DARLING (3) followed an unplaced effort first-up two runs back with a second last start over 1000m at Deniliquin. Finds a tougher race but she has the talent to test this line-up. NODDY'S GIRL (4) hasn't got warm in three runs, but is in a new stable and the recent jumpouts hint at an improved showing.",
